# 7. BACKEND AND DATABASE REQUIREMENTS

Before implementing database changes, inspect the existing Supabase schema and backend architecture.

Use the existing Supabase project and configuration.

Do not create a second Supabase project.

Do not modify or rename existing Properties or Interior tables.

Create dedicated Loans tables.

Implement secure server-side APIs for:

- Creating a public loan enquiry.
- Listing loan enquiries for authorised CRM staff.
- Fetching a loan enquiry by ID.
- Updating enquiry status.
- Assigning staff.
- Recording call logs.
- Scheduling follow-ups.
- Retrieving dashboard metrics.

### Public API security

The public form should have access only to the operation needed to submit a new enquiry.

Public users must not be able to:

- Read other enquiries.
- Read customer records.
- Read internal notes.
- Change enquiry statuses.
- Access CRM staff information.
- Modify existing records.

Validate and sanitise all incoming data on the server.

Apply suitable rate limiting and spam protection to the public enquiry endpoint.

Use existing server-side privileged database access patterns securely. Never expose Supabase service-role keys or other private secrets to frontend code.

If database row-level security is used, configure it consistently with the existing architecture and test it.

Do not weaken security policies on existing tables.

### Duplicate enquiry handling

Implement sensible duplicate handling.

If the same customer submits another enquiry, do not silently discard it.

Preserve the new enquiry or associate it with the existing customer according to the chosen data model.

Record the new enquiry and its source accurately.

Do not merge unrelated customers solely because they share a name.

